The Bounded Dream Rehearsal implementation follows the algorithm described by
Nijjer et al. in arXiv:2607.19749 and the Apache-2.0 reference artifact at
https://github.com/gurpnijjer/dream-rehearsal, inspected at commit
7680778f798be3a27a17c320cc875b573c45f0e1. That original bounded port does not
execute the reference source; its provenance and deviations are documented in
docs/protocols/bounded_dream_rehearsal_atari.md.

The separate official-code reference includes unmodified selected source from
Dream Rehearsal under Apache-2.0 and NM512 DreamerV3 under the MIT License,
copyright (c) 2023 NM512. See third_party/dream_rehearsal/LICENSE,
third_party/dream_rehearsal/UPSTREAM.md, third_party/nm512_dreamerv3/LICENSE,
and third_party/nm512_dreamerv3/UPSTREAM.md. These sources are not relabeled
as project-original code.

The paired-history collection adapter follows NM512 tools.simulate's
MIT-licensed collection semantics; its attribution is retained in
scripts/dream_rehearsal_collection.py and third_party/nm512_dreamerv3/LICENSE.

